  "problem": "Models could receive the entire corpus, be asked to guess a missing publisher document, lose table headers across pages, double-count overlapping chunks, or be asked to authorize access. Incomplete context could be forced to completion.",
  "resulting_behavior": "classifyResidualType separates prose definition, table extraction, scientific ambiguity, missing evidence and access blockade. Only prose definition and table extraction are routine model extraction; scientific ambiguity is an adjudication proposal. A missing publisher document abstains and cannot be converted into a guess. chunkPassages preserves table headers, denominators, page positions, field context and overlap identity so a multi-page table does not lose its header/denominator and overlapping chunks cannot double-count a field. Accepted tasks have source bytes and a stable ID. Oversized or low-information cases return to parsing. Incomplete context abstains rather than forcing completion. No task processes the entire corpus. Models are never asked to authorize access or establish endpoint availability.",
